From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:05:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Small fixes from the 2026-11-16 review: forwarded addresses,
 plugin message data, spectate, scratch lists, resource pack answers

- A forwarded address that is not an IP address is refused: new InetSocketAddress looked it up in
  DNS on the event loop, before the BungeeGuard token was checked (L1).
- A plugin message's data is a heap copy of its own: the pooled buffer readBytes(int) took was given
  back only by the handler, so a packet dropped before it kept it from the pool (L3).
- Spectating looks only at the worlds this thread ticks: another thread's entity map is not this
  one's to read (L4).
- A query's scratch list is taken inside the try, so a query that throws still gives it back (L5).
- The resource pack answer runs on the player's tick thread: its event is a synchronous one (L10).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

